083 decode-grouped-tile: wider KV tile for the grouped Triton decode kernel

Stage 1 of the grouped decode kernel walks the KV 32 keys per loop step on 4 warps.
Under the fp32 softmax.V dot (patch 011) that tile is compute-bound: a deep KV reads at
about half of the GA102 bandwidth ceiling (459 GB/s of 889 on Gemma 4 31B's 512-wide
global layers at 223K). SGLANG_TRITON_DECODE_GROUPED_BLOCK_N / _NUM_WARPS set the tile
and warp count (0 / unset = upstream). Arithmetic is unchanged; only the fp32
accumulation order moves (rel-L2 4e-4 vs the 32-key tile). A shape whose tile overflows
shared memory at compile time is remembered and keeps the upstream 32 x 4 tile.
gemma4-31b 64 x 8: 35.6 -> 41.8 tok/s at 223K, 54.4 -> 55.4 at 37K.
flint 128 x 4: 115.0 -> 123.9 tok/s at 241K, flat at 34K.
